-- 043: Deep content + matching exercises for X07 · Introduction to Power BI.
UPDATE public.sessions SET
 content_en = E'## From spreadsheet to living dashboard\n\nPower BI turns a static export into a **dashboard that updates itself** and that stakeholders can explore. This lesson takes you from importing data to a published, shareable report.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Power BI workflow\n\n`Get Data → Transform (Power Query) → Model (relationships) → Visualize → Publish`\n\n| Stage | What you do | Where |\n|-------|-------------|-------|\n| Get Data | Connect Excel/CSV/database | Home → Get Data |\n| Transform | Clean, rename, set types | Power Query Editor |\n| Model | Link tables on keys | Model view |\n| Visualize | Drag fields onto visuals | Report view |\n| Publish | Push to the cloud | Power BI Service |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Core visuals\n\n| Visual | Use for |\n|--------|---------|\n| **Card** | A single KPI (Total Revenue) |\n| **Bar / Column** | Comparison across categories |\n| **Line** | Trend over time |\n| **Table / Matrix** | Detailed or cross-tabbed numbers |\n| **Map** | Values by geography |\n\nDrag a field into the **Values** well to aggregate it; drag one into **Axis/Legend** to split it.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Building the dashboard\n\n- **Relationships**: in Model view, link `orders[customer_id]` to `customers[id]` so a region slicer filters revenue correctly.\n- **Cross-filtering**: click a bar and every other visual filters to it automatically — Power BI''s superpower.\n- **Slicers**: add a Region or Date slicer so viewers filter without editing anything.\n- **Layout**: KPIs across the top, supporting charts below, one clear title.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Measures & DAX (a first taste)\n\nA **measure** is a reusable calculation written in **DAX**:\n\n```\nTotal Revenue = SUM(orders[total_amount])\nAvg Basket = DIVIDE([Total Revenue], DISTINCTCOUNT(orders[id]))\n```\n\nMeasures recalculate with every filter and slicer click — that is what makes the dashboard interactive.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Publish & share\n\n**Publish** → Power BI Service → put the report in a **Workspace** → share with named people or a link. Set a **scheduled refresh** so the data stays current without manual re-export.\n\n> **Mini case study.** TokoSegar''s weekly deck used to take 3 hours of copy-paste. Rebuilt as one Power BI report with a scheduled refresh, it now updates itself every Monday morning — the analyst just adds a one-line commentary.\n\n---\n\n## Common pitfalls\n\n- **No relationships defined** → slicers filter one table but not the others.\n- **Importing dirty data** → clean in Power Query first, not with hacks in visuals.\n- **Dashboard overload** → 20 visuals on one page answers nothing; one page, one question.\n- **Forgetting scheduled refresh** → a "live" dashboard silently goes stale.\n\n---\n\n## Glossary\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| Power Query | Power BI''s data-cleaning/transform step |\n| Relationship | A link between two tables on a key |\n| Cross-filtering | Clicking one visual filters the others |\n| Measure | A reusable DAX calculation |\n| Power BI Service | The cloud where reports are published & shared |\n\n---\n\n## Key Takeaways\n\n1. The flow is **Get Data → Transform → Model → Visualize → Publish**.\n2. Define **relationships** so slicers and cross-filtering work across tables.\n3. Use **cards** for KPIs, bar/line for comparison/trend; keep one question per page.\n4. **Measures** in DAX recalculate on every filter — the source of interactivity.\n5. **Publish** to a Workspace and set a **scheduled refresh** to keep it live.\n\n> 💡 Practice with the matching exercises below, then build a dashboard for the assignment case.',
 content_id = E'## Dari spreadsheet ke dashboard hidup\n\nPower BI mengubah ekspor statis menjadi **dashboard yang memperbarui dirinya** dan bisa dieksplorasi stakeholder. Pelajaran ini membawa Anda dari mengimpor data hingga laporan yang dipublikasikan dan bisa dibagikan.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Alur kerja Power BI\n\n`Get Data → Transform (Power Query) → Model (relasi) → Visualize → Publish`\n\n| Tahap | Yang Anda lakukan | Di mana |\n|-------|-------------------|---------|\n| Get Data | Hubungkan Excel/CSV/database | Home → Get Data |\n| Transform | Bersihkan, rename, set tipe | Power Query Editor |\n| Model | Tautkan tabel lewat kunci | Model view |\n| Visualize | Tarik field ke visual | Report view |\n| Publish | Dorong ke cloud | Power BI Service |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Visual inti\n\n| Visual | Untuk |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Card** | Satu KPI (Total Revenue) |\n| **Bar / Column** | Perbandingan antar kategori |\n| **Line** | Tren seiring waktu |\n| **Table / Matrix** | Angka detail atau cross-tab |\n| **Map** | Nilai berdasarkan geografi |\n\nTarik field ke well **Values** untuk mengagregasi; tarik ke **Axis/Legend** untuk memecahnya.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Membangun dashboard\n\n- **Relasi**: di Model view, tautkan `orders[customer_id]` ke `customers[id]` agar slicer region memfilter revenue dengan benar.\n- **Cross-filtering**: klik satu bar dan setiap visual lain otomatis memfilter — kekuatan super Power BI.\n- **Slicer**: tambah slicer Region atau Date agar penonton memfilter tanpa mengedit apa pun.\n- **Layout**: KPI di atas, chart pendukung di bawah, satu judul jelas.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Measure & DAX (cicipan pertama)\n\n**Measure** adalah perhitungan yang bisa dipakai ulang, ditulis dalam **DAX**:\n\n```\nTotal Revenue = SUM(orders[total_amount])\nAvg Basket = DIVIDE([Total Revenue], DISTINCTCOUNT(orders[id]))\n```\n\nMeasure dihitung ulang setiap kali filter dan slicer diklik — itulah yang membuat dashboard interaktif.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Publish & bagikan\n\n**Publish** → Power BI Service → taruh laporan di **Workspace** → bagikan ke orang tertentu atau via link. Atur **scheduled refresh** agar data tetap terkini tanpa ekspor ulang manual.\n\n> **Studi kasus mini.** Deck mingguan TokoSegar dulu butuh 3 jam copy-paste. Dibangun ulang sebagai satu laporan Power BI dengan scheduled refresh, kini ia memperbarui diri setiap Senin pagi — analyst tinggal menambah komentar satu baris.\n\n---\n\n## Kesalahan umum\n\n- **Tidak mendefinisikan relasi** → slicer memfilter satu tabel tapi tidak yang lain.\n- **Mengimpor data kotor** → bersihkan di Power Query dulu, bukan akal-akalan di visual.\n- **Dashboard berlebihan** → 20 visual dalam satu halaman tak menjawab apa pun; satu halaman, satu pertanyaan.\n- **Lupa scheduled refresh** → dashboard "live" diam-diam jadi basi.\n\n---\n\n## Glosarium\n\n| Istilah | Arti |\n|---------|------|\n| Power Query | Langkah pembersihan/transform data Power BI |\n| Relasi | Tautan antara dua tabel lewat kunci |\n| Cross-filtering | Klik satu visual memfilter yang lain |\n| Measure | Perhitungan DAX yang bisa dipakai ulang |\n| Power BI Service | Cloud tempat laporan dipublikasikan & dibagikan |\n\n---\n\n## Kesimpulan Utama\n\n1. Alurnya **Get Data → Transform → Model → Visualize → Publish**.\n2. Definisikan **relasi** agar slicer dan cross-filtering bekerja lintas tabel.\n3. Pakai **card** untuk KPI, bar/line untuk perbandingan/tren; satu pertanyaan per halaman.\n4. **Measure** DAX dihitung ulang tiap filter — sumber interaktivitas.\n5. **Publish** ke Workspace dan atur **scheduled refresh** agar tetap live.\n\n> 💡 Latih dengan exercise matching di bawah, lalu buat dashboard untuk case tugas.'
WHERE session_number = 'X07';

INSERT INTO public.exercises (session_id, type, title_en, title_id, description_en, description_id, starter_code, solution_code, test_cases, hints_en, hints_id, difficulty, order_num)
SELECT s.id, 'matching', 'Power BI Workflow', 'Alur Kerja Power BI',
  'Match each workflow stage to what happens there.', 'Cocokkan setiap tahap alur dengan yang terjadi.',
  '{"pairs":[{"left":"Get Data","right":"Connect to a source"},{"left":"Power Query","right":"Clean and set data types"},{"left":"Model view","right":"Link tables on keys"},{"left":"Publish","right":"Push the report to the cloud"}]}','',
  '[{"id":"tc1","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Connect to a source","description_en":"Get Data","description_id":"Get Data","points":25},{"id":"tc2","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Clean and set data types","description_en":"Power Query","description_id":"Power Query","points":25},{"id":"tc3","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Link tables on keys","description_en":"Model","description_id":"Model","points":25},{"id":"tc4","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Push the report to the cloud","description_en":"Publish","description_id":"Publish","points":25}]',
  '["Power Query is the cleaning step","Model view is where relationships live"]','["Power Query langkah pembersihan","Model view tempat relasi"]','easy',1
FROM public.sessions s WHERE s.session_number='X07' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.exercises e WHERE e.session_id=s.id AND e.title_en='Power BI Workflow');

